------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=45 Human bait
Text=We have...used some. In attempt to draw out the creature that was preying on them, we left some humans as bait. We waited, and thought that once the beast appeared we would easily deal with it...but that hasn't been the case. In every instance, the fiend has managed to seize the bait and escape. 
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=What is the beast like?
Go to node ID=50 The facelessness of the beast

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=You used humans as bait?
Go to node ID=46 Fishermen use worms

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=I have nothing more to say to you. 
Go to node ID=100 Goodbye
Icon=Exit Icon
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=46 Fishermen use worms
Text=Do not human fishermen use worms to draw a fish? It is the same principle, surely you understand. 
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=That is truly evil.
Go to node ID=46 More worms

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=What is the beast like?
Go to node ID=50 The facelessness of the beast
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=46 More worms
Text=What? It was just a few humans, there are plenty more. And we did it partly for them, the creature was eating them, anyway. We were trying to protect them by capturing the beast.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=That's truly evil, monster.
